 > The effect is to get a floating exception in main/newgame/mklev/add_door,
 > right after the "Go bravely with Jehovah! --more--". Well, not right after, 

You should probably turn off vision_tables when you make such a large
map.  I have played 80x50, and got some strange vision from time to time.
(Sometimes seeing the walls of undiscovered rooms that later proved
 to be closed, no line of sight.)
It got a bit boring, lots of rooms to discover, lots of gold.  Experience came
faster as I spent more time on each level.  (I usually discover all rooms
before going down.)  If you want a balanced game, you should limit the number 
of levels so that the area & volume of the dungeon remains the same.

